	(descr "4mm metal dome contact, two-pad land. Sits under the centre of the trackball unit so pressing the ball closes it. Pad 1 is the switched line, pad 2 the dome skirt, which is grounded. No courtyard: this land lives inside the ball unit's own footprint by design, so the ball's courtyard is the one that has to be kept clear, and a courtyard here would only report the overlap it is meant to have. Dimensions are a generic 4mm dome land and are UNVERIFIED against a part in hand.")
